# Deploy

Push `main` → **CI** passes → deploy workflow v8 (`workflow_run`). Skill: `deploy`.

**The user runs the push** (`20-git-push-policy.mdc`) — the agent never pushes, so it never starts a deploy.

Secret: `SSH_PRIVATE_KEY`. Optional vars: `DEPLOY_HOST`, `DEPLOY_USER`, `DEPLOY_PORT`.

Port/runtime → **`12-production-port.mdc`** (do not duplicate port rules here).

| Step | Command |
|------|---------|
| Sync + deploy | `bash deploy/remote-deploy.sh` (on VPS or via Actions) |
| Stop before build | `pm2 stop darulquran-next` (inside remote-deploy.sh) |
| Install & build | `npm ci` → `npm run build` |
| Start | `pm2 start ecosystem.config.cjs --update-env` |
| Health | curl `LOCAL_URL` from `deploy/runtime.cjs` + sample chunk |

Critical: stop PM2 **before** touching `.next`. Verify chunk URL after restart. Apache serves `/_next/static/`.  
Failed deploy: `remote-deploy.sh` rolls back git + restarts previous PM2 — confirm health URL before leaving the session.

Never `rm -rf .next` while PM2 is serving. Confirm Node on VPS matches `engines` / CI (**24.17.x**).

## CI (GitHub Actions)

On PR + `main`: `lint` → `check:urdu` → `test` → `npm audit --audit-level=critical` → `build`

Dependabot: `.github/dependabot.yml` (weekly)

Audit gate is **critical** (matches CI + `techstack.md`). Transitive **high** advisories in Sanity CLI / ESLint toolchain are accepted; never `npm audit fix --force` (downgrades Sanity to v5).

## Production env checklist

After deploy, verify VPS `.env` includes (see `.env.example`):

- `REVALIDATE_SECRET` + Sanity webhook (`setup-revalidation` skill)
- `RESEND_API_KEY` + `EMAIL_TO` (or legacy `EMAIL_*` SMTP)
- Optional: `UPSTASH_*`, Turnstile keys

Security: **`17-security.mdc`**
